    {"id":"6f7ca5dd-7e3c-48ec-9b4f-4e711e3a591c","name":"Sticky Note","type":"n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote","typeVersion":1,"position":[-48,48],"parameters":{"content":"## Clinic Telegram Bot (TEMPLATE — do not activate directly)\nThis is the reference workflow backend/app/core/n8n_client.py::clone_telegram_workflow() clones per Telegram channel. It rewrites two placeholders on every clone:\n- \"Normalize & Config\" assignment channelId -> the real channel UUID\n- \"Outbound Send Webhook\" path -> a unique per-channel path\n...and swaps every telegramTrigger/telegram node's credential for the channel's own bot token.\n\nInbound photos: \"Has Photo?\" branches to \"Upload Photo To Storage\" (uploads the Telegram-downloaded binary to the Supabase Storage `chat-media` bucket) before falling through to \"Normalize & Config\", which also computes the public media_url/media_type passed to the backend and to ai-services.\n\nInbound voice notes: \"Has Voice?\" (checked when there's no photo) branches to \"Download Voice\" (Telegram file get, using the channel's own bot credential) then \"Upload Voice To Storage\", setting media_type=audio so ai-services transcribes it via Gemini instead of the AI turn seeing an empty message and escalating unnecessarily.\n\nOutbound QR image: after \"Generate AI Reply\", \"Has QR Image?\" checks for a booking-confirmation `image_url` and, if present, fetches it with the shared X-Service-Token and relays it back to the patient as a real photo via \"Send QR Photo\".\n\nSet this workflow's ID as N8N_TELEGRAM_TEMPLATE_WORKFLOW_ID in the backend env. Replace the REPLACE_WITH_* placeholders (backend/ai-services URLs, SERVICE_TOKEN, Supabase project ref + service key) before activating any clone.","color":5,"height":420,"width":460}}
